639	    /**
640	     * The number of owners a city must already contain before it is flagged as approaching its
641	     * capacity limit. Once a city holds at least this many owners (but is not yet at
642	     * {@link #CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY}), the create and read responses report {@code capacityWarning}
643	     * true for owners in that city.
644	     */
645	    private static final long CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40L;
646	
647	    /**
648	     * Reports whether the given city is approaching its capacity limit, i.e. whether it already
649	     * contains between {@link #CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD} and {@link #CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY}
650	     * minus one owners (40 to 49) inclusive. The count is taken the same way the hard rejection
651	     * counts a city's owners ({@link #countOwnersInCity(String)}). A {@code null} city never warns.
652	     *
653	     * @param city the city to test, or {@code null}
654	     * @return {@code true} when the city holds 40 to 49 owners, otherwise {@code false}
655	     */
