724	    /**
725	     * Flags a newly created owner as a possible (soft) duplicate. Reaching this point means the
726	     * owner already cleared {@link #rejectDuplicateIdentity(OwnerFieldsDto)}, so it does not share
727	     * an existing owner's identity key. A member that declared its household via
728	     * {@code sharesHousehold} is a deliberate addition to a known household, not a suspected
729	     * duplicate, so it is never flagged. Otherwise it is a possible duplicate when an existing owner
730	     * shares the Soundex code of its {@code lastName} and its {@code postcode} while carrying a
731	     * different identity key (see {@link #findPossibleDuplicate(Owner)}). When such an owner is
732	     * found, {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code true} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} to the
733	     * matching owner's id; otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is set {@code false} and no matching
734	     * id is recorded. An owner without a postcode can share no postcode and is never a possible
735	     * duplicate.
736	     *
737	     * @param owner the owner being created, already carrying its normalized telephone and postcode
738	     * @param ownerFieldsDto the submitted owner fields carrying the {@code sharesHousehold} flag
739	     */
740	    private void applyPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner, OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
741	        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
742	        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
743	        if (sharesHousehold(ownerFieldsDto)) {
744	            return;
745	        }
746	        findPossibleDuplicate(owner).ifPresent(existing -> {
747	            owner.setPossibleDuplicate(true);
748	            owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(existing.getId());
749	        });
750	    }
